<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Junius Brutus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Junius Brutus was the legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>. According to Roman tradition he led the revolt that expelled the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquinius Superbus</a>, in 509 BCE and became one of the first two consuls. Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> honoured him as a model of devotion to liberty, and he was said to have had his own sons executed for plotting to restore the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucius-junius-brutus.jpg" alt="Lucius Junius Brutus" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M._Junius_Brutus,_denarius,_54_BC,_RRC_433-2_(obverse_L._Junius).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
